{"key": "KXRECBASELINE|Will the Republican reconcilliation bill be scored relative to a current policy baseline?|If the Congressional Budget Office scoring documents evaluate the next reconciliation bill that becomes law relative to a current policy, rather than current law, baseline, then the market resolves to Yes.", "decision": "NO", "confidence": 0.92, "reasoning": "The next Republican reconciliation bill to become law was H.R. 1 (the \"One Big Beautiful Bill Act\"), enacted July 4, 2025. CBO's official cost estimate, dated July 21, 2025, evaluated this law \"Relative to CBO's January 2025 Baseline,\" which is a current law baseline. CBO is statutorily required to use a current law baseline (where expiring provisions expire as written). The resolution criterion required scoring relative to a current POLICY baseline (where expiring provisions continue). Since CBO used a current law baseline, the YES condition was not met. The resolution is NO.", "sources": ["https://www.cbo.gov/topics/budget/reconciliation", "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61537", "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61474", "https://www.brookings.edu/articles/what-are-budget-baselines-and-what-do-they-have-to-do-with-reconciliation-in-congress/"], "queries": ["Republican reconciliation bill 2025 CBO score", "reconciliation bill current policy baseline CBO 2025", "\"One Big Beautiful Bill\" CBO final score enacted law baseline", "CBO H.R. 1 2025 reconciliation current law baseline official estimate"], "links": ["https://www.conference-board.org/research/CED-Newsletters-Alerts/cbo-scores-house-reconciliation-bill", "https://www.thefiscaltimes.com/newsletter/20250604-Republican-Tax-Bill-Will-Add-24-Trillion-Deficit-CBO", "https://www.thefiscaltimes.com/2025/06/13/Chart-Day-CBO-Report-Card", "https://doggett.house.gov/media/press-releases/senate-republican-health-repeal-bill-making-america-uninsured-again", "https://www.dailysignal.com/?p=63448", "https://www.dailysignal.com/2025/06/04/price-tag-big-be